# Discover DFW — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit real values; .env*
# (except this file) is gitignored. Production values live in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.

# ---- Supabase (auth + database) ----
# From Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API Keys.
# URL + publishable key are safe to expose (RLS is the boundary).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# SERVER-ONLY — bypasses RLS; used for lead tables, lead emails, and the
# alert sweep. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never committed.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---- MLS (Trestle IDX Plus / NTREIS) ----
# "trestle" serves live inventory; unset/"mock" serves fictional data
# (mock mode also re-noindexes every search surface automatically).
MLS_PROVIDER=trestle
# SERVER-ONLY. From Trestle → Products → <product> → Feeds → Manage.
# The credential expires yearly — RESET there, update here + Vercel.
# (TRESTLE_CLIENT_ID / TRESTLE_CLIENT_SECRET are accepted as aliases;
#  TRESTLE_TOKEN_URL / TRESTLE_ODATA_BASE_URL override the endpoints.)
# Smoke test: node scripts/trestle-smoke.mjs [city]
TRESTLE_API_ID=
TRESTLE_API_PASSWORD=

# ---- Email (Resend) ----
# SERVER-ONLY. Sending key; mail goes out as alerts@discoverdfw.com.
# Without it, every send degrades to a server log (nothing crashes).
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Internal lead notifications (showing requests, questions) go here —
# the owner/broker/team inbox. Unset = guide notifications are skipped;
# user confirmation emails still send.
LEAD_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# Dev safety: outside production, all emails DRY-RUN (logged, not sent)
# even with a real key. Set to 1 only to deliberately send from dev.
EMAIL_SEND_IN_DEV=

# ---- Admin ----
# Comma-separated emails allowed into /admin/leads (the Lead Desk).
# A visitor must hold a real session AND be on this list; unset = the
# admin surface 404s for everyone. Upgrade path: profiles.role column.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# ---- Cron ----
# Shared secret guarding /api/alerts/run — Vercel Cron sends it
# automatically when the same value exists as a Vercel env var.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 24
CRON_SECRET=

# Optional overrides
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.discoverdfw.com
